# VIntObj_RunList with more than 3 objects on the V-int list (ruling 5, 2; $008AFE-$008B1E: the
# walk's 5th to 8th unrolled units and the loop back), at its first call: 8 more objects are made
# as 8 VIntObj_NewIdle calls would make them (each pops the pool head, takes handler
# VIntObj_IdleHandler $8BEC and is linked before the tail sentinel g_VIntListTail;
# g_ObjPoolFree - 8), so the list is the run's own objects (none at the TAS's first V-int), the
# 8, the sentinel. An idle handler is the object's state until its creator stores its own (the
# V-int can land between), and stands in for whatever handlers a longer list holds. The reference never had more than 3
# (Stage2_RunLift's flush + lift scroll + a VM6 job); every VIntObj_New / NewIdle site is one-shot
# per scene except the VM6 clear/blit jobs, freed only by their own end, so a longer list needs
# VM6 jobs started while others are in flight: undetermined (NOTES, Open questions: cov10
# "VIntObj_RunList", cov12). The lines below are cov17_vint.py 8 (scratchpad).

